WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.060
Do you trust your gut?

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.349
Imagine you've been saving up money for a while,

00:00:03.349 --> 00:00:07.019
so you visit the bank ready to make your first major investment.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:09.796
You talk with an advisor, and after a few minutes,

00:00:09.796 --> 00:00:13.080
they tell you about a plan that you feel is extremely risky.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.537
You ask them why,

00:00:14.537 --> 00:00:16.499
and they just say they have a good feeling about it.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:17.860
Would you feel safe?

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.240
Of course not.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.030
Which is why we use data strategies.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.584
This is simply an understanding of our personal objectives,

00:00:24.584 --> 00:00:26.575
collecting data and then managing

00:00:26.575 --> 00:00:29.940
and analyzing it to ensure that it aligns with these objectives.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.490
Gone are the days of simply trusting your gut.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.250
Today, businesses work with data analysts,

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:38.271
engineers and scientists to form these data strategies

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.990
leading to better outcomes.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.985
So by understanding them, you can position yourself for success

00:00:43.985 --> 00:00:47.344
and make a meaningful contribution to the world of data and analytics,

00:00:47.344 --> 00:00:48.810
even in your personal life.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:50.903
To learn more about all things data,

00:00:50.903 --> 00:00:53.070
head on over to the Data Differentiator,

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.889
IBM's Guide for Data Leaders and enthusiasts alike.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.250
We hope to see you there.

